```java
@Transactional
public BindingView bind(CreateBindingRequest request) {
    // 1. idempotent replay check
    Optional<TaskBinding> existing = bindingRepository.findByRequestId(request.requestId());
    if (existing.isPresent()) {
        TaskBinding b = existing.get();
        if (b.taskId() == request.taskId() && b.calibrationId() == request.calibrationId()) {
            return bindingViews.of(b);
        }
        throw ApiException.conflict("REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT", ...);
    }
    // 2. load task & calibration
    ReceiveTask task = taskRepository.findById(request.taskId()).orElseThrow(404);
    // 3. lock antenna row
    antennaRepository.lockById(task.antennaId());
    // 4. lock calibration row & re-read
    AntennaCalibration cal = calibrationRepository.findByIdForUpdate(request.calibrationId()).orElseThrow(404);
    // 5. validations
    if (cal.antennaId() != task.antennaId()) 422 ANTENNA_MISMATCH
    if (cal.status() == INVALIDATED) 422 CALIBRATION_INVALIDATED
    if (!cal.passed()) 422 CALIBRATION_NOT_PASSED
    if (task.startTime().isBefore(cal.validFrom()) || task.endTime().isAfter(cal.validUntil())) 422 TASK_WINDOW_OUTSIDE_VALIDITY
    // 6. existing current binding for task
    Optional<TaskBinding> current = bindingRepository.findCurrentByTaskId(task.id());
    if (current.isPresent() && current.get().status() == BOUND) throw 409 TASK_ALREADY_BOUND;
    // 7. overlap
    List<TaskBinding> overlaps = bindingRepository.findActiveOverlapping(task.antennaId(), task.startTime(), task.endTime());
    if (!overlaps.isEmpty()) throw 409 ANTENNA_OCCUPIED;
    // 8. supersede old pending binding
    current.ifPresent(b -> bindingRepository.markSuperseded(b.id()));
    // 9. insert
    TaskBinding binding = new TaskBinding(null, request.requestId(), task.id(), cal.id(), task.antennaId(),
        cal.azimuthDeviationDeg(), cal.elevationDeviationDeg(), BindingStatus.BOUND, false, Instant.now(clock));
    try {
        long id = bindingRepository.insert(binding);
    } catch (DuplicateKeyException e) {
        // concurrent same requestId committed between check and insert
        TaskBinding winner = bindingRepository.findByRequestId(request.requestId()).orElseThrow(...);
        if (winner.taskId() == request.taskId() && winner.calibrationId() == request.calibrationId()) return bindingViews.of(winner);
        throw ApiException.conflict("REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT", ...);
    }
    return bindingViews.of(... with id);
}
```

Wait — DuplicateKeyException inside a @Transactional method: after a constraint violation, in H2 the transaction may still be usable (H2 doesn't abort the whole tx on statement failure, unlike PostgreSQL). Catching and continuing to read within the same tx should work in H2 and MySQL (InnoDB also allows continuing after duplicate key error). OK.

Note the ordering: idempotency check first means a replay with same params returns 200 even if... fine.

Also "校准被复核作废时…不能利用已作废记录抢占天线" — covered by status check under row lock. The race: invalidate tx locks calibration row first, bind waits, then sees INVALIDATED → 422. Or bind locks first, binds, commits; invalidate then demotes/flags. Consistent either way.

One issue: `findByIdForUpdate` when calibration doesn't exist → no row locked, return 404. Fine.

404 check for calibration should happen before antenna lock? Order doesn't matter much. But note: if calibration doesn't exist, we throw 404 — good.

Edge: task window validation when cal not passed → validFrom null; check passed first, so NPE avoided.

Also the requestId replay check happens before task/calibration existence checks. If requestId exists → return/conflict. Good.

Now BindingService implementation.

