Idempotency: bind req-1 → 201; bind req-1 same params → returns same binding id (status 201 again since controller always returns 201... hmm. Replay returns 201 Created again — acceptable? Ideally 200. The controller has @ResponseStatus(CREATED) always. For replay, returning 201 with same body is tolerable but 200 is more correct. To differentiate, controller could check... simpler: keep 201 for both, test asserts same binding id and only one row in DB. That's fine and defensible. Actually let me make replay return 200: BindingController can't easily know. I could have service return a small wrapper... Keep it simple: 201 both times; assert identical id and count==1. Fine.

异参 409: req-1 with different calibrationId → 409 REQUEST_ID_CONFLICT.

失败不占键: bind req-x with task outside validity → 422; then create valid task and bind req-x → 201.

Frozen snapshot: cal1 dev 0.10/-0.08 → bind task → binding shows 0.10/-0.08, calibrationId=cal1. Create cal2 (newer, dev 0.15) → binding unchanged (GET task → bindings[0] still cal1, 0.10).

